cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "Preemptive Peak Power Scheduling with A Priori Certificates: code and experiments"
abstract: >-
  Certify-Round-Improve (CRI) framework for the preemptive Peak Power Minimization Scheduling
  Problem (PPMSP): a priori certificates on the optimal peak, certified roundings, local searches,
  exact models, the baselines of the paper, the numerical verification of the theory, and the
  complete experimental campaign with its statistical report.
